      "message": "there is actually a tiny hole here, if we enable vconn and vbus is low, we drop down to the else case. but, if the vbus interrupt occurs before we set delayed_vconn, then we will miss our chance to set vconn. so, i think we actually want:\n\n/* record to turn it on later when VBUS appears */\ndelayed_vconn \u003d enable ? polarity : -1;\n\n/* Never turn on VCONN before seeing VBUS */\nif (!enable || gpio_get_level(CHGR_ACOK))\n\t/* Set VCONN on the opposite CC line from the polarity */\n\tgpio_set_level(polarity ? GPIO_USBC_VCONN1_EN_L :\n\t\t\t\t  GPIO_USBC_VCONN2_EN_L, !enable);",
